            <ArticleTitle>[The oral cavity: what shall we look for--and what can we do?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3016-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients present with symptoms of the oral cavity at their general practitioner (GP). As a general rule, the GP should refer the patient to a dentist for diagnosis and treatment. However, treatment of acute infections can be started by the GP. In the present paper, the diagnosis and treatment of such cases is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
